[center][size=6][b][color=#e5793a]Idle Life[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4]Somewhere to be, for everyone around you.[/size][/center]

Bethesda hand-placed every spot where people warm their hands, lean or sit, so most places have few. Idle Life gives the people near you new places to spend their time, each kind where it belongs: warming their hands at fires, coffee at counters, leaning on real walls, a sitting circle round a campfire. Placed at run time, gone when you leave.

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-idle-life@ead5dc83679dd2e26f8d5a9c1a324c7a7dbc48e3/docs/img/rule.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Placed the way Bethesda places them.[/b] Measured from the game's own spots: hands warmed 69 units from the fire, campfire sitters 131 out. People stay a minute or so, then move on by themselves.[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-idle-life@ead5dc83679dd2e26f8d5a9c1a324c7a7dbc48e3/docs/img/navmesh.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Walls, read from the navmesh.[/b] Papyrus can't see geometry, so a small F4SE plugin reads the ground the game walks on: real walls, and no spots over a drop.[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-idle-life@ead5dc83679dd2e26f8d5a9c1a324c7a7dbc48e3/docs/img/budget.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Enough to feel alive, never a field of props.[/b] 1.5 spots per person, 3 to 40, drawn across 17 kinds to fit the place.[/center]

[size=4][b][color=#e5793a]Every kind of spot[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Fires and campfires, counters, tables and benches, rails and walls, open ground.
[*]Workbenches by type: power armor, chems, tools.
[*]Radios (dancing), pool tables, TVs, gates.
[*]Robots and dogs: Mr Handy gets some gardening and hedge trimming.
[*]Spots next to people that suit the place: raiders with Jet and knives, settlers with clipboards, townsfolk with newspapers and their Pip-Boy.
[*]At night, fires and radios draw more people.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#e5793a]Settings (MCM)[/color][/b][/size]
Spots per person, the maximum, a daily reshuffle, a switch for each kind, and a Testing page (spawn test settlers, status).

[size=4][b][color=#e5793a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]F4SE
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url] (one plugin for every game version)
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/21497]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] (optional, for the settings)
[/list]
Fallout 4 1.10.163, Next-Gen or the Anniversary Edition. No masters beyond Fallout4.esm; the DLC are used when you have them. Without F4SE or Runtime Database only the spots along walls and in the open are off, and Idle Life says so in game. Install with Vortex or MO2: the installer checks your setup first. Manual installs are not supported.

IdleLife.dll is [url=https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/465127378f44a7003b35330a4f931ce295ef0327f23eccf6991f1e85248f632c]clean on VirusTotal[/url] (0/75). Licence: PolyForm Noncommercial.
